\"fastqc\",\n            \"output\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"data\",\n                \"input\": [\n                  {\"src\": \"hda\", \"id\": \"FASTQC_RAW_DATA_1\"},\n                  {\"src\": \"hda\", \"id\": \"FASTQC_RAW_DATA_2\"}\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n\n  By default this waits for the job and, in JSON mode, refreshes output\n  state/type/size so agents do not need follow-up job/dataset show calls. Use\n  --no-wait only when you intentionally want asynchronous submission.\n\n  Use --dry-run-payload or --save-payload PATH to inspect the exact POST body\n  after dataset and collection references have been normalized.\n\n  Use `tool show <tool_id>` only when task files do not provide enough input\n  names/options to build the submission JSON.\n\nOptions:\n  --history-id TEXT\n  -i, --input TEXT         Tool input as key=value\n  --inputs-json FILE       Path to JSON file with tool inputs. Keys are input\n                           names; values may be nested dicts/lists for repeats\n                           and conditionals. -i flags override.\n  --wait / --no-wait       Wait for job completion and refresh output\n                           metadata. Default: --wait.\n  --timeout INTEGER        Max wait time in seconds (default: 1800)\n  --poll-interval INTEGER  Seconds between status checks (default: 180)\n  --dry-run-payload        Print the exact Galaxy POST body and do not submit\n                           the tool.\n  --save-payload FILE      Write the exact Galaxy POST body to PATH before\n                           submitting.\n  --help                   Show this message and exit.\n---\nUsage: galaxy-cli history [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...\n\n  Manage Galaxy histories.\n\nOptions:\n  --help  Show this message and exit.\n\nCommands:\n  copy    Copy an existing history and set the copy as the current...\n  create  Create a new history and set it as the current working history.\n  delete  Delete a history.\n  export  Start exporting a history archive.\n  list    List histories.\n  show    Show history details.\n  update  Update history metadata and sharing flags.\n  use     Set the current working history.\n---\nUsage: galaxy-cli history copy [OPTIONS] HISTORY_ID [NAME]\n\n  Copy an existing history and set the copy as the current working history.\n\n  Examples:\n    galaxy-cli history copy abc123\n    galaxy-cli history copy abc123 \"working copy\"\n    galaxy-cli history copy abc123 \"working copy\" --all-datasets\n\nOptions:\n  --all-datasets  Also copy deleted datasets and deleted collections\n  --help          Show this message and exit.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
